{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And sought to kill.</b> They handed him over to a sardiot to kill him, but the sword had no power over him. And our Rabbis, blessed be their memory, said that his neck became like a pillar of marble. And a hint to this: there was no need to write anything other than 'ויברח' — 'וישב משה' — the extra letters, and they are in gematria 'אבן שיש' (marble stone). And further, they said in the Midrash that Gabriel came and put the face of the sardiot onto Moses' face, and took the sword from his hand and killed him instead of Moses, and they were thus convinced that Moses had been killed, and he fled. Another interpretation: they brought Moses up onto a platform to kill him, and the Holy One, blessed be He, made Pharaoh mute, and the deputies deaf, and the speculators blind, and Moses fled. As it is said: ״מי שם פה לאדם״ — when Pharaoh said to kill Moses: who made him mute, that he did not persist in the order? And the deputies deaf, that they did not hear the order? And the speculator blind? And who made you perceptive to flee from them? And Jethro received him into his house. From here you learn that whoever undertakes to perform a mitzvah, that mitzvah does not depart from him — for Jethro received into his house Moses, who fled from the enemy to save him, and from him descended one who received an enemy who fled from the blood-avenger to kill him — and which one was this? Sisera, to the tent of Jael of the children of Berak, and he was killed there."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The phrase מהה\"ר משה appears to attribute the gematria observation to 'the honor of our master Rabbi Moses'; translated the abbreviation as an attribution tag left implicit. The text is dense and unvocalized; some run-on interpretations have been separated following the apparent logical breaks."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:35.715675166Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}